# File formats and exporting

Deliver each illustration in a format people can open, and keep the files you need to change it later.

<h2 id="bg-ill-10">Choose the format</h2>

| Use | Format | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Guidance pages and dashboards | SVG | Keep it small. Remove hidden layers and editor data. Set a `viewBox` so it scales. |
| Social media posts | PNG | Export at the size the platform asks for, at twice the pixel density for sharp screens. |
| Photographs | JPEG or WebP | Photographs are not illustrations. See [Icons and images](images.html#images). |
| Editable source | The design tool’s own file | Keep it with the asset. Do not ask people to open it to see the illustration. |

## Put the file in Home Assistant

Put files in the `www` folder inside your configuration folder. Home Assistant serves them from `/local/`, so `www/illustrations/hall-sensor.svg` becomes `/local/illustrations/hall-sensor.svg`.

## Record the asset

For each new Civica asset, record the editable source, author, licence, purpose, alternative text decision and intended background in `docs/data/illustration-assets.json`. The [artwork register](../reference/documentation-artwork.json) holds the same details for section headers.

## Check the file

Check the exported file:

- at small and large sizes
- on light and dark backgrounds
- with images switched off
- with a colour blindness simulator

A file that opens without errors has not passed an accessibility check. Record what you tested and anything still to fix in `docs/data/brand-guidance-checklist.json`.
